      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785969945681,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) How to achieve low latency (<200ms) feed requests?\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) How to achieve low latency (<200ms) feed requests?\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "8db2y3c30Tt2SdJGKeY5i",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 999.0226925028568,
      "y": 566.2567736904392,
      "width": 971.359130859375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1504791216,
      "version": 239,
      "versionNonce": 467145296,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785970212600,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Real time cache feed with CDC (Change data capture)\n- Data Collection Service stores new articles in the database, which triggers CDC events. \nThese CDC events are consumed by Feed Generation Workers that immediately determine which regional feeds need updates,\n based on the article's region and relevance.  => new article added with timestamp to maintain order\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Real time cache feed with CDC (Change data capture)\n- Data Collection Service stores new articles in the database, which triggers CDC events. \nThese CDC events are consumed by Feed Generation Workers that immediately determine which regional feeds need updates,\n based on the article's region and relevance.  => new article added with timestamp to maintain order\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "y7LqiSBUqC1Z6y1FnJ8TL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 999.6360018531336,
      "y": 677.5383480240006,
      "width": 425.79156494140625,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 877947472,
      "version": 78,
      "versionNonce": 930956464,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785970259771,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) Ensure articles appear within 30mins of publication?\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) Ensure articles appear within 30mins of publication?\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Uyh-vh3mOoS8YuwNVwZFP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 999.4461680066192,
      "y": 713.7771425701189,
      "width": 1172.54296875,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b06",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1456341168,
      "version": 146,
      "versionNonce": 692697168,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785971287676,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- build a webhook endpoint at POST /webhooks/article-published that publishers can call the moment they publish an article, \ncontaining the article metadata or even the full content payload. instead of us trying to find new articles, we can rely on them telling us about them!\n- Falling back to RSS polling and web scraping for publisher not supporting webhook",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- build a webhook endpoint at POST /webhooks/article-published that publishers can call the moment they publish an article, \ncontaining the article metadata or even the full content payload. instead of us trying to find new articles, we can rely on them telling us about them!\n- Falling back to RSS polling and web scraping for publisher not supporting webhook",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
