      "updated": 1785971281223,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5) Handle traffic spikes during breaking news?\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5) Handle traffic spikes during breaking news?\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "76jFuVB-zQJZFnqIHbt2R",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 993.4055576598453,
      "y": 935.478737626137,
      "width": 1187.503173828125,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0B",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1846658736,
      "version": 297,
      "versionNonce": 1028428976,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785971624486,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Feed Service (application layer) - horizonal scaling with auto scaling group\n- DB layer: I/O subsystem, network bandwidth and CPU resources all become bottleneck\n- Cache layer (redis) - by location, pre-computed regional feeds. \nUse consistent hashing to shard the data across multiple instances and ensure each instance has a replica or two to handle the read load and failover.\n- Shard READ data\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Feed Service (application layer) - horizonal scaling with auto scaling group\n- DB layer: I/O subsystem, network bandwidth and CPU resources all become bottleneck\n- Cache layer (redis) - by location, pre-computed regional feeds. \nUse consistent hashing to shard the data across multiple instances and ensure each instance has a replica or two to handle the read load and failover.\n- Shard READ data\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7HmirrD2yuJ3RYr3UglKg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1018.3273344329984,
      "y": 1061.3337103305607,
      "width": 634.0315551757812,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1296732848,
      "version": 14,
      "versionNonce": 1597322416,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785971649196,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6) How can we support category-based news feeds (Sports, Politics, Tech, etc.)?\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6) How can we support category-based news feeds (Sports, Politics, Tech, etc.)?\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pE0zz6-edWP_myLUz3YnF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1005.8664460464217,
      "y": 1093.7320201356602,
      "width": 1020.9591064453125,
      "height": 260,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 335723600,
      "version": 54,
      "versionNonce": 2127813200,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785971723334,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- in-memory filtering. When we cache articles in feed:US, instead of storing just article IDs as members, \nwe store complete article metadata as JSON strings. Each cached article includes all the information needed for category filtering\n - title, description, URL, category, region, and publication timestamp.\n{\n  \"id\": \"123\",\n  \"title\": \"NBA Finals Game 7 Results\",\n  \"description\": \"Warriors defeat Celtics in thrilling finale\",\n  \"url\": \"https://espn.com/nba/finals/game7\",\n  \"category\": \"sports\",\n  \"region\": \"US\",\n  \"published_at\": \"2024-06-21T22:30:00Z\"\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- in-memory filtering. When we cache articles in feed:US, instead of storing just article IDs as members, \nwe store complete article metadata as JSON strings. Each cached article includes all the information needed for category filtering\n - title, description, URL, category, region, and publication timestamp.\n{\n  \"id\": \"123\",\n  \"title\": \"NBA Finals Game 7 Results\",\n  \"description\": \"Warriors defeat Celtics in thrilling finale\",\n  \"url\": \"https://espn.com/nba/finals/game7\",\n  \"category\": \"sports\",\n  \"region\": \"US\",\n  \"published_at\": \"2024-06-21T22:30:00Z\"\n}\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6BXjofuHyq1yNZvqX1cE1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1026.0880630238394,
      "y": 1373.2870464842085,
      "width": 200.8318328857422,
      "height": 40,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
